#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0280 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "LBREASND is not in the dataset at all while LBSTAT says NOT DONE -- the guarded variable's column is ABSENT ENTIRELY. Under EC-43 an absent column is all-missing, so empty(<var>) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports its defect on the rows its other conjuncts select. The variable was removed from Requirements.Variables.All on 2026-08-27 (owner ruling) because it is Permissible in this domain and NO rule anywhere reports its absence -- neither a specific presence rule nor the generic Required/Expected rules, which do not cover Permissible variables. Before that removal this scenario would have taken a silent dataset SKIP."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBSTAT   type=Char label="Completion Status"
---
S1 | LB | 001 | 1 | ALB | NOT DONE
